From 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] QCLINUX: soc: qcom: make QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG user-selectable

QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG is a promptless tristate enabled only via "select" from
DRM_MSM. On a headless build the GPU/DRM stack is disabled, so nothing selects
it and <linux/soc/qcom/ubwc.h> compiles the stub whose
qcom_ubwc_config_get_data() returns -EOPNOTSUPP. The downstream Iris video
codec (iris-video-dlkm) treats that as fatal and fails to probe, even though
the sc7280/qcm6490 UBWC data and driver are already in-tree.

Give the symbol a prompt so it can be enabled from a config fragment
independently of DRM_MSM.

Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [gives a promptless symbol a prompt for the out-of-tree iris-video-dlkm]
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/Kconfig
@@ -298,7 +298,7 @@ endmenu
 endmenu

 config QCOM_UBWC_CONFIG
-	tristate
+	tristate "Qualcomm UBWC configuration data"
 	help
 	  Most Qualcomm SoCs feature a number of Universal Bandwidth Compression
 	  (UBWC) engines across various IP blocks, which need to be initialized
